35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The reviews show that shared spaces are loved, while isolated ones are ignored.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The timetable data is brutal. Every closure forces us to rent off-site space.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The diaries confirm it. Weather eats six weeks. Delivery data shows comfort projects always slip.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The tenders show plant costs jumped twenty percent. The reserve for old AV gear is empty.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The freeze left us short on hands, but the technicians have spare hours.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, if comfort projects slip, we should avoid anything that needs long outdoor work.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, exactly. And the booking data shows general rooms are always full.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, yes. But if we pick a project that relies on weather, we lose the year.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, and if we pick plant work, the budget is already wrong. The reserve is a trap.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the reserve is empty, but the technicians are bored. We can use them.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,The older blocks are a minefield. Hazardous material means months of delay.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,The specialist rooms are empty. Why are we spending money on them?,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The delivery data is clear. Only inspection-driven work finishes on time.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,The market has moved. Our paper figures are dead. We need a plan that is cheap and fast.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The manual routines are the key. We can automate the boring parts and free up the staff.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,We need a project that is useful to everyone and does not depend on the weather.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,The general rooms are the only ones with real demand. The data is clear.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"If we pick a project that is already delayed, we are just adding to the pile.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"The budget is the only thing that is real. If the numbers do not work, the project is dead.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"The staff are the only resource we have. If we do not use them, we are wasting them.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
